    {
      "code": "run_aborted",
      "collection": "codes",
      "fields": [
        {
          "path": "args.bars_count",
          "beforePresent": false,
          "afterPresent": true,
          "before": null,
          "after": {
            "kind": "integer",
            "optional": true
          }
        },
        {
          "path": "args.strategy_started",
          "beforePresent": false,
          "afterPresent": true,
          "before": null,
          "after": {
            "kind": "boolean",
            "optional": true
          }
        },
        {
          "path": "description",
          "beforePresent": true,
          "afterPresent": true,
          "before": "The run was aborted on request.",
          "after": "The run was aborted on request. Cooperative SIGTERM stops after the in-flight input bar completes, leaves no sink trailer, and exits 1. bars_count is the nonnegative number of fully completed input bars, mirrored as top-level bars.count, matching the runner's bars_processed population; strategy_started is a boolean mirrored at the top level. Both are optional for legacy abort raisers. There is no cancelled class: the abort path has exactly two internal callers, the orchestrator's hand-off at the service limit (the run is restarted with the same run id) and an operator stop. The abort line itself carries no retry semantics: it has no retryable field, and a retry is APP's decision from which caller stopped the run. On the abort path bars_count is diagnostic only and is never billed. No live-counter descriptor is used (fd 6 is not used)."
        }
      ]
    },
